// The classes the library adds to: what is iterable, an array of it, text (an array of characters), a number, a character
// (a number), a program, a diagnostic.
Iterable := class { }
// A list, an Array: entered at its first vertex (`head`; the last, `tail`), each vertex holding a value (`value`, `next`,
// `previous`); what a list is written as (`[a, b]`, `a, b`). What it answers as an Iterable (`first`, `count`, `for`, …) is
// Ray.ray's; the kernel's map (`wasm.o.ray`) walks its vertices faster.
Array := class: Iterable { }
Array &+= {
  new => Array &+ {
    head := None
    tail := None
    listing := true
    spread := false
    // (a list as a type, `{d: "0".."9"}`: what reads as one of its values, that value)
    {written} => (.).one_written(`{written}`)
